  "question_stem": "The polynomial $6x^3 + ax^2 + bx + 9$ is denoted by $p(x)$, where $a$ and $b$ are constants. It is given that $(x - 3)$ is a factor of $p(x)$, and when the first derivative $p'(x)$ is divided by $(x - 3)$ the remainder is 72.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$p(x)=6x^3-11x^2-24x+9$ and $x-3$ is a factor.",
    "$p(x)=(x-3)(2x+3)(3x-1)$"
  ],
